{"audit_run_id":"audit:9548f9a0a8604ba99f783a200d18d31a","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":57,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"`hedge_sections.csv` — 40 data rows plus one header row."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"One row is one surveyed farm hedge section: a 50 metre length of lowland farm hedge, surveyed once"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"in early winter and measured for all five outcomes. There are 40 sections in total, 20 cut every"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"year and 20 cut once every three years on rotation. Every section has a value for every outcome, so"},{"end_column":30,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"there are no missing entries."},{"end_column":35,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"| Column | Type | Unit | Meaning |"},{"end_column":26,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":107,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"| `section_id` | text | — | Short per-section identifier, `hs01` to `hs40`, unique to one hedge section. |"},{"end_column":178,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| `cut_regime` | text | — | Cutting regime the section is under. Exactly two values: `annual` (cut every year) and `rotational` (cut once every three years). 20 sections each. |"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| `berry_mass_gpm` | number | grams per metre of hedge | Declared outcome 1. Autumn berry dry mass. |"},{"end_column":130,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| `stem_density_spm` | number | stems per metre of hedge | Declared outcome 2. Woody stem density measured at one metre height. |"},{"end_column":124,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `plant_richness_spp` | integer | species count | Declared outcome 3. Vascular plant species richness in the hedge base. |"},{"end_column":167,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `basal_gap_pct` | number | percent of section length | Declared outcome 4. Basal gap length: the share of the 50 m section with no woody cover below half a metre. |"},{"end_column":156,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `invert_biomass_mgpm` | number | milligrams per metre of hedge | Declared outcome 5. Overwintering invertebrate biomass from a standard beating sample. |"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"Outcome columns appear in the pre-declared order 1 to 5. Rows are in survey order, so the two"},{"end_column":53,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"cutting regimes are interleaved rather than blocked."},{"end_column":31,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"| Column | Minimum | Maximum |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":35,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"| `berry_mass_gpm` | 10.4 | 96.0 |"},{"end_column":36,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"| `stem_density_spm` | 7.1 | 18.2 |"},{"end_column":34,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"| `plant_richness_spp` | 7 | 20 |"},{"end_column":33,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"| `basal_gap_pct` | 3.5 | 32.8 |"},{"end_column":41,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| `invert_biomass_mgpm` | 14.7 | 137.5 |"}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:9604e99761022816419e","parser_version":"0.