{"audit_run_id":"audit:9548f9a0a8604ba99f783a200d18d31a","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":95,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"The analysis uses `hedge_sections.csv`. One row is one surveyed farm hedge section, a 50 metre"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"length of lowland farm hedge surveyed once in early winter and measured for all five outcomes."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"There are 40 sections, 20 cut every year and 20 cut once every three years on rotation, with no"},{"end_column":16,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"missing values."},{"end_column":21,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"| Column | Meaning |"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"| --- | --- |"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"| `section_id` | Short per-section identifier, `hs01` to `hs40`. |"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"| `cut_regime` | Cutting regime: `annual` or `rotational`, 20 sections each. |"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"| `berry_mass_gpm` | Autumn berry dry mass, grams per metre of hedge. |"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"| `stem_density_spm` | Woody stem density at one metre height, stems per metre of hedge. |"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"| `plant_richness_spp` | Vascular plant species richness in the hedge base, species count. |"},{"end_column":106,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"| `basal_gap_pct` | Basal gap length, percent of section length with no woody cover below half a metre. |"},{"end_column":126,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"| `invert_biomass_mgpm` | Overwintering invertebrate biomass from a standard beating sample, milligrams per metre of hedge. |"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"Each of the five pre-declared outcomes was compared between the two cutting regimes with a"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"two-sample t-test for independent groups, giving one raw p-value per outcome. The five declared"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"outcomes were then corrected together as one family with the statistics library's default"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"multiple-comparisons correction at a family-wise error level of 0.05. All five raw p-values were"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"passed to that routine in a single call, and every significance verdict below comes from the"},{"end_column":52,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"routine's output rather than from the raw p-values."},{"end_column":43,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"Outcomes are listed in the declared order."},{"end_column":83,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"| Outcome | Mean (annual) | Mean (rotational) | Raw p | Adjusted value | Verdict |"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":69,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"| `berry_mass_gpm` | 24.73 | 60.73 | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | significant |"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"| `stem_density_spm` | 13.66 | 11.65 | 0.0162 | 0.0634 | not significant |"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| `plant_richness_spp` | 11.25 | 13.80 | 0.0173 | 0.0634 | not significant |"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"| `basal_gap_pct` | 18.42 | 15.18 | 0.1448 | 0.2686 | not significant |"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"| `invert_biomass_mgpm` | 50.02 | 43.27 | 0.3598 | 0.3598 | not significant |"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"The berry mass raw p-value is 1.01e-07 and its adjusted value is 5.06e-07; both round to 0.0000 in"},{"end_column":17,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"the table above."},{"end_column":25,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"Per-outcome conclusions:"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"1. Berry mass: rotationally cut sections carried about 36 g per metre more autumn berry dry mass"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":47,"start_column":4,"start_line":47,"text":"than annually cut sections, and this difference survives the family-wise correction."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"2. Stem density: annually cut sections were about 2.0 stems per metre denser, but after correcting"},{"end_column":49,"end_line":49,"start_column":4,"start_line":49,"text":"the family the difference is not significant."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"3. Plant richness: rotationally cut sections had about 2.6 more species in the hedge base, again"},{"end_column":37,"end_line":51,"start_column":4,"start_line":51,"text":"not significant after correction."},{"end_column":88,"end_line":52,"start_column":1,"start_line":52,"text":"4. Basal gap: annually cut sections had about 3.2 percentage points more basal gap, not"},{"end_column":33,"end_line":53,"start_column":4,"start_line":53,"text":"significant after correction."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"5. Invertebrate biomass: annually cut sections were about 6.7 mg per metre higher, not significant"},{"end_column":21,"end_line":55,"start_column":4,"start_line":55,"text":"after correction."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"The one result that holds up across the whole family of five outcomes is autumn berry supply."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"Sections cut on a three year rotation produced roughly two and a half times the berry dry mass of"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"sections cut every year, which matters directly for overwintering birds and small mammals that feed"},{"end_column":19,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"on hedgerow fruit."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":64,"start_column":1,"start_line":64,"text":"The other four outcomes moved in the directions you might expect, with annual cutting giving denser"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"stems and rotational cutting giving slightly richer hedge bases, but none of those differences is"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"strong enough to stand once the five declared outcomes are corrected together. Section to section"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"variation in this survey is wide, so with 20 sections per regime these smaller effects cannot be"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"separated from ordinary field scatter. They should be treated as unresolved rather than as evidence"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"that no difference exists."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":71,"start_column":1,"start_line":71,"text":"Practical advice from this single winter survey: moving hedges onto a three year cutting rotation is"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"supported by the berry result. Claims about stem density, base flora, basal gaps, or invertebrate"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"biomass are not supported by these data either way, and would need a larger or repeated survey to"},{"end_column":8,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"settle."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:9a80a1defab1b4132104","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:4276ee2767b2b3af89ee7920c278e084144f9f645f01f085f3be04b5933dc1a2","end_line":74,"locator":"report.md:1-74","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
